---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArrowIcon from '../components/ArrowIcon.astro';
import SectionEyebrow from '../components/SectionEyebrow.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Home" navCurrent="home">

  {/* ── Hero ─────────────────────────────────────────────── */}
  <header class="hero">
    <div>
      <div class="hero-eyebrow">
        <span class="eyebrow">Melbourne · 6 weeks – 6 years</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="display">
        A village where<br />
        every child <em>belongs</em>.
      </h1>
      <p class="lede">
        A Melbourne childcare centre that takes the best of how children are
        raised around the world — play and nature, real foundations, the
        confidence to be seen — and builds it into one place where every child
        is known.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-ctas">
        <a href="/book-a-tour" class="btn-primary">
          Book a Tour
          <ArrowIcon />
        </a>
        <a href="/philosophy" class="btn-secondary">Read our philosophy</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-art">
      <div class="hero-art-bg"></div>
      <div class="hero-floater">
        <span class="eyebrow">From a parent</span>
        <p>"It's the only place I've toured where I didn't have to choose between play and rigour."</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  {/* ── At a glance strip ────────────────────────────────── */}
  <section class="strip">
    <div class="strip-inner">
      <div class="strip-item">
        <span class="eyebrow">Ages</span>
        <span class="val">6 weeks – 6 years</span>
      </div>
      <div class="strip-item">
        <span class="eyebrow">Hours</span>
        <span class="val">7:00am – 6:30pm</span>
      </div>
      <div class="strip-item">
        <span class="eyebrow">Framework</span>
        <span class="val">EYLF · NQF aligned</span>
      </div>
      <div class="strip-item">
        <span class="eyebrow">Location</span>
        <span class="val">Inner Melbourne</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ── Philosophy intro ─────────────────────────────────── */}
  <section class="section" id="philosophy">
    <div class="section-head">
      <SectionEyebrow number="01" label="Our approach" />
      <h2 class="display">
        Children learn best when they're <em>guided</em> &mdash; and when they're <em>trusted to lead</em>.
      </h2>
    </div>
    <div class="philosophy-grid">
      <div>
        <p>
          Some of the day here is <strong>structured</strong> — early literacy and
          numbers, music, movement, the small daily routines that build focus
          and confidence.
        </p>
        <p>
          The rest is <strong>child-led exploration</strong> — open-ended time
          where children follow their own curiosity, and we follow with them.
        </p>
        <div class="pull-quote">
          <p>School-ready. Life-ready.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>
          We lead with exploration on purpose. Structure has clear strengths,
          and we use it deliberately. But the qualities that stay with a child
          for life — <strong>curiosity, resilience, imagination, the ability to
          get along with others</strong> — grow most when children have the freedom
          to wonder, try, fail, and try again.
        </p>
        <p>
          So we build the day around play and inquiry, and bring structure in
          where it genuinely helps.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ── Three things (courage · curiosity · belonging) ────── */}
  <section class="minds">
    <div class="minds-inner">
      <div class="section-head">
        <SectionEyebrow number="02" label="What every child takes with them" />
        <h2 class="display">
          Three things, learned <em>every day</em>, in every part of the day.
        </h2>
      </div>
      <div class="three-up">
        <div class="mind">
          <span class="num">i.</span>
          <h3>Courage</h3>
          <p class="promise">The nerve to keep going — and to be <em>seen</em>.</p>
          <p>
            When a tower of blocks falls for the third time, we don't rush in
            to rebuild it. We stay close, and let the child discover they can
            try again — and we make being seen, and getting it wrong, feel
            safe. Courage is both.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="mind">
          <span class="num">ii.</span>
          <h3>Curiosity</h3>
          <p class="promise">Knowing <em>how</em> to learn — and wanting to.</p>
          <p>
            We care less about a child having the right answer and more about
            what they do when they don't have one yet. Asking a question,
            making a guess, testing it, being wrong, and trying another way —
            that's the muscle we strengthen every day.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="mind">
          <span class="num">iii.</span>
          <h3>Belonging</h3>
          <p class="promise">At home with <em>yourself</em>, and with others.</p>
          <p>
            A child who can say "I'm frustrated" instead of grabbing, or who
            notices a friend left out and brings them in — and who feels proud
            of where they come from and wholly at home here — is learning
            something as important as any letter or number.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ── EXPLORE methodology ─────────────────────────────── */}
  <section class="explore-section" id="curriculum">
    <div class="section">
      <div class="section-head">
        <SectionEyebrow number="03" label="How we teach" />
        <h2 class="display">
          Seven things we look for in every <em>child-led moment</em>.
        </h2>
      </div>
      <p class="explore-intro">
        Exploration here is intentional, not accidental. Our educators plan for
        it, watch closely, and shape it as it unfolds. We call the approach
        <strong>EXPLORE</strong>.
      </p>
      <div class="explore-list">
        <div class="explore-item">
          <div class="explore-letter">E</div>
          <div class="explore-content">
            <h4>Enquiry</h4>
            <p class="promise">It starts with a question.</p>
            <p>When a child asks why worms come out after rain, we head outside to find out together.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="explore-item">
          <div class="explore-letter">X</div>
          <div class="explore-content">
            <h4>e<em class="x-tail">X</em>perience</h4>
            <p class="promise">Children learn by doing, not by watching.</p>
            <p>Rather than demonstrate how a seed grows, we give children soil, water, and seeds.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="explore-item">
          <div class="explore-letter">P</div>
          <div class="explore-content">
            <h4>Purpose</h4>
            <p class="promise">The work matters to the child.</p>
            <p>Caring for the class garden or setting the table gives children genuine responsibility.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="explore-item">
          <div class="explore-letter">L</div>
          <div class="explore-content">
            <h4>Leadership</h4>
            <p class="promise">Every child gets to lead.</p>
            <p>A three-year-old showing a younger friend how to wash the paintbrushes is learning to guide.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="explore-item">
          <div class="explore-letter">O</div>
          <div class="explore-content">
            <h4>Open-ended creativity</h4>
            <p class="promise">There's no single right outcome.</p>
            <p>With blocks, clay, paint, and loose parts, children invent their own solutions.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="explore-item">
          <div class="explore-letter">R</div>
          <div class="explore-content">
            <h4>Reflection</h4>
            <p class="promise">We pause to make sense of it.</p>
            <p>At the end of a project, we ask "What did you discover?" — turning experience into understanding.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="explore-item">
          <div class="explore-letter">E</div>
          <div class="explore-content">
            <h4>Empathy</h4>
            <p class="promise">We learn to see through another's eyes.</p>
            <p>When two children want the same toy, we treat it as a chance to practise listening and finding a fair way forward.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ── A day here ──────────────────────────────────────── */}
  <section class="day" id="day">
    <div class="day-grid">
      <div class="day-text">
        <SectionEyebrow number="04" label="A day here" />
        <h2 class="display">Calm and purposeful. <em>Never chaotic.</em></h2>
        <p>
          Structure gives the day its rhythm. Exploration gives it its spark.
          Outdoor time isn't squeezed in — it's a core part of how children
          learn here, every day.
        </p>
        <p>
          Your child will be known, challenged at the right level, and free to
          follow the questions that light them up.
        </p>
        <a href="/book-a-tour" class="day-link">
          Come and see a day in person
          <ArrowIcon size={14} />
        </a>
      </div>
      <div class="day-images">
        <div class="day-img day-img-1" data-label="outdoor exploration"></div>
        <div class="day-img day-img-2" data-label="structured time"></div>
        <div class="day-img day-img-3" data-label="reflection & story"></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ── Testimonial ─────────────────────────────────────── */}
  <section class="testimonial">
    <div class="testimonial-inner">
      <blockquote>
        "He comes home talking about <em>what he discovered</em>, not just what he did. That's the difference."
      </blockquote>
      <cite>— Parent of a 4-year-old, Carlton</cite>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ── Final CTA ───────────────────────────────────────── */}
  <section class="final-cta" id="book">
    <h2 class="display">Come and <em>see for yourself</em>.</h2>
    <p>
      Tours run weekday mornings. Allow about 40 minutes — enough to walk
      through, meet a few educators, and watch the day unfold.
    </p>
    <a href="/book-a-tour" class="btn-primary">
      Book a Tour
      <ArrowIcon />
    </a>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>
